WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.770
Around Strangford Lough in County Down,
the land rises in swarms of small, oval

2
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.890
hills.

3
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.630
A Royal Geographical Society
guide calls them a basket of eggs.

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.430
Each hill is typically
250 to 1,000 metres long.

5
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.410
Hedges and fields
criss-cross their slopes.

6
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.670
For the people who farm,
live and visit here,

7
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.550
are these hills a gift, or a problem?

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.690
In this mission, you'll find out
what these hills are made of,

9
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.730
and why they line up.

10
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.130
Then you'll weigh up what this landscape
means for the people who use it.

11
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.350
Your mission: decide whether County Down's
drumlin landscape is a gift or a problem

12
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.110
for the people who live there.
